## 4️⃣ launchd plist – run as a *daemon* that survives reboots

Save this as **`/Library/LaunchDaemons/com.mycompany.filewatcher.plist`** (system‑wide) or `~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.mycompany.filewatcher.plist` (per‑user). The system‑wide variant runs as **root** – perfect for watching files that only root can access.

```xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN"
        "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!-- Human‑readable keys -->
    <key>Label</key>               <string>com.mycompany.filewatcher</string>

    <!-- Program to launch -->
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/usr/local/bin/FileWatcher</string> <!-- compiled binary -->
    </array>

    <!-- Run early, stay alive -->
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>           <true/>
    <key>KeepAlive</key>           <true/>

    <!-- Restart on crash or when the system reboots -->
    <key>WatchPaths</key>          <array>
                                        <string>/path/to/watch/dir</string>
                                   </array>

    <!-- Defensive: Time‑based constraints (optional) -->
    <key>StartInterval</key>       <integer>120</integer>   <!-- fallback poll every 2 min -->

    <!-- Permissions – requires root for launchd system daemon -->
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>     <string>/var/log/com.mycompany.filewatcher.out</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>   <string>/var/log/com.mycompany.filewatcher.err</string>

    <!-- Make sure we clean up resources on termination -->
    <key>UserName</key>            <string>root</string>
    <key>ThrottleInterval</key>    <real>0.5</real>
</dict>
</plist>
```

